guamp: every distinct problem of a Metal process to the kernel log in pieces (Maps "null buffer", fin48)

fin48 (kpan-20261105-151331): Maps died at 446.8 s on "VectorKit received null buffer from Metal"; the kernel saw only its first
problem's 46 characters ("native-metal: commandBuffer refused: command b"). The buffer refusals and the reason of the refused
command buffer never reached any log the board keeps. Each distinct problem (at most 24 a process, "no device answer" left out) now
goes out as "problem pr<k> <38 characters>", up to 6 pieces. NMB_PROBLEMS_TO_KERNEL=0 (guamp-m2v-env) turns it off.
Applies after 0001-0003, 0009-0019 and 0030; the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI.

diff --git a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
index 3f2161e..b0bade9 100644
--- a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
+++ b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
@@ -453,7 +453,23 @@ static char gLastProblems[2][200];
 static char gFirstProblem[200];
 // Called once with the first problem, on the thread that hit it: a polling reader missed WidgetRenderer's, which crashed within its first second.
 void (*native_bridge_metal_problem_hook)(const char *);
+// guamp (UniXNU-guamp patches/adreno-metal/0020): every distinct problem's whole text to the kernel, not only the first problem's 46
+// characters: "problem pr<k> <38 characters>", up to 6 pieces, at most 24 problems a process (native-adreno 0009 prints them as
+// "GuampMetal: client <process>: ..."). fin48: Maps died on "VectorKit received null buffer from Metal" after "commandBuffer refused:
+// command b...", and neither the buffer refusals nor the command buffer's reason reached any log. NMB_PROBLEMS_TO_KERNEL=0 turns it off.
+static void forwardProblem(const char *text) {
+ static const bool on=[]{const char *v=getenv("NMB_PROBLEMS_TO_KERNEL");return !v || strtoul(v,nullptr,0)!=0;}();
+ if(!on || !text || !native_bridge_metal_problem_hook || !strncmp(text,"native-metal: no device answer",30))return;
+ static std::mutex lock;static std::set<std::string> said;
+ {std::lock_guard<std::mutex> guard(lock);if(said.size()>=24 || !said.insert(text).second)return;}
+ const size_t length=strlen(text);
+ for(unsigned k=0;k<6 && (size_t)k*38<length;k++) {
+  char line[48];snprintf(line,sizeof line,"pr%u %.38s",k,text+(size_t)k*38);
+  native_bridge_metal_problem_hook(line);
+ }
+}
 static void noteProblem(NSString *what) {
+ forwardProblem(what.UTF8String);
  gProblems++;
  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(gProblemLock);
  // A device answer the runtime lacks is reported at creation in every process and is harmless: the first problem is the next one.
